+
+## L9: balanced constraint supervision, local preparation only
+
+L9 asks whether replacing L8's lexical-heavy auxiliary set with a high-confidence, more balanced set improves generalization while holding the L6 training recipe and **25%** constraint exposure fixed. No GPU run has occurred: the previous A40 was deleted and the current RunPod pod list is empty. All corpus curation, adversarial review, automatic validation, implementation, and local tests were completed before stopping at that resource boundary. The exact commands and post-training decision procedure are in `L9_RUNBOOK.md`.
+
+The reviewed L9 pool has **101 proposed examples**. Every complete source target was read internally, including the rejected proposals. Decisions were **82 GOOD, 3 REVISE, 16 REJECT**, leaving **85** final prompt variants from **60/84** training works: **18 lexical prohibitions, 32 spatial/relation, 25 indirect/exclusion, and 10 mixed**. The 16 rejections include weak semantic links, overclaimed locations or emotions, and examples that would reward a missing label while stating the concept directly. The three revisions repaired ambiguous actor assignments or overstrong claims without changing targets. `l9_constraint_proposals.json`, `l9_constraint_review.json`, and `l9_constraint_final.json` preserve each source target ID/hash, original and proposed prompts, structured constraint, paraphrased evidence, adverse reading, deterministic checks, and review outcome. Full target text stays in ignored `data/l9/constraints.jsonl` and `outputs/l9-private-review.json`, never in the tracked metadata. The original L5 train SHA-256 remains `a5c3cb2ef60b1fae7e8d11a956c96935f518ae3fb047636000dc327937ca7608`; L9 derived rows hash to `c23e959ff5d4074570665d9fde15c2e3cabcd58541e94ae1b55052e49f511954`.
+
+The final set reuses each target **once**, reaches at most **three variants per work**, and contains **66 descriptive / 19 sparse** origins with length buckets **11 very short, 34 short, 32 medium, 8 longer**. Case-insensitive whole-word and common-form checks pass for all 53 examples with a lexical or implied-concept exclusion. All 42 spatial/mixed examples have explicit subject–predicate–object relation metadata and matched source-evidence markers; marker presence is only a deterministic aid, so all 42 still require the recorded full-target semantic review. No final prompt shares more than four consecutive normalized words with its target, and no final prompt equals a fixed50 or novel20 evaluation prompt. The complete machine report is `l9_qa.json`; it records **zero errors**. These are internal judgments, not independent human ratings.
+
+The L9 sampler is the L8 sampler with only the replacement constraint set: seed **314162**, constraint seed **314170**, two L9 variants plus six unchanged L4-weighted originals per effective batch of eight. The deterministic planned 40-step trace has **80/320 = 25%** auxiliary draws: **16 lexical, 28 spatial/relation, 25 exclusion, 11 mixed**. Its full-plan hash is `0b440adda50173ae5d8ba1785b88f13a8ba347c33037d77da5aaf4cf31b57d95`. The local `l9_baseline_lock.json` verifies unchanged fixed and novel prompt hashes and saved baseline generations; it carries forward the prior internal fixed passes **B0 5/17, L1 4/17, L6 4/17, L8 4/17** and novel passes **L1 3/20, L6 2/20, L8 2/20**, without rescoring them. These are **scheduled counts and historical baselines**; actual L9 exposure, smoke, wall time, checkpoints, fixed and novel constraint results, writing quality, memorization, blind review, and any promotion decision remain unmeasured until a real A40 run. L9's planned matched checkpoints are **25, 35, 40**; step 50 requires a concrete health reason, and no L9b is permitted.
+
+`python3 -m scripts.pipeline`, `python3 -m scripts.build_l5`, `python3 -m scripts.build_l9`, `python3 -m scripts.qa_l9`, and `python3 -m scripts.lock_l9_baselines` completed; the source tree and old L5 dataset hash were unchanged. The local suite reports **24 passed, 3 skipped**. L1/L6/L8 adapters and fixed generations are present locally, as are the unchanged fixed50 and novel20 prompt files. The pinned base revision is listed upstream but is not cached locally; the replacement A40 must fetch it. No model weights or secrets will be committed, and no push or publication has occurred. **Next required action:** connect a replacement A40, execute the two-update smoke, then the single 40-step L9 run and its locked evaluations. No L10 experiment is justified before those results.
